From 6207068ea3f14550bf4f2c479840b94e9bf1d144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 07:18:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Harden free tools + tune for Railway basic (low-RAM) tier

OOM prevention (basic tier):
- Global PIL decompression-bomb cap (MAX_IMAGE_MPX, default 40Mpx) so a
  20MB upload can no longer decode to multi-GB RGBA and kill the worker
- rembg model preload is now opt-in (REMBG_PRELOAD); lazy-load by default
  so the container does not OOM at boot before serving a request
- ML/IO thread pools env-configurable; ML workers default to 1
- Dockerfile pins OMP/OpenBLAS/MKL/onnxruntime threads to 1
- bgremove downscales oversized inputs (BGREMOVE_MAX_DIM, default 2000px)
- pdf2img/OCR clamp per-page pixmap render so a huge MediaBox cannot OOM

Correctness / robustness fixes:
- OCR: resolve Tesseract languages against installed packs (eng fallback)
  instead of crashing when uzb/rus missing; add subprocess timeout
- mergepdf: keep all sources open until after save (avoids lazy-ref
  corruption) and close every handle in finally (no QPDF leak on error)
- pdf2img: reject non-PDF uploads with 422 and map ValueError to 422
- translate: cumulative deadline so the MyMemory fallback cannot exceed
  the outer budget; argostranslate gated behind ARGOS_TRANSLATE
- unzip: add uncompressed-size and bomb-ratio guards to the 7z path

Document new env vars in .env.example.
